<?php

namespace App\Support;

class LegalPolicyTemplates
{
    /** Reviewed starting points, deliberately unpublished until the operator confirms the facts. */
    public static function documents(): array
    {
        return [
            'terms-and-conditions' => ['title' => 'Terms & Conditions', 'draft_content' => self::terms()],
            'privacy-policy' => ['title' => 'Privacy Policy', 'draft_content' => self::privacy()],
        ];
    }

    private static function terms(): string
    {
        return <<<'HTML'
<p>These Terms govern your use of [APP_NAME], operated by [OPERATOR_NAME]. The service connects campaign owners with people who choose to share promotional material and submit evidence of its performance. By registering or using the service, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the service. Please also read our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
<h2>1. Eligibility and your account</h2>
<p>You must be at least 18 years old and legally able to enter an agreement. Provide accurate registration, contact, location and payment information, keep it current, and protect your password and verification codes. Do not sell accounts, impersonate another person, create fake referrals, or use someone else's payment details without permission. Tell support if your account is compromised.</p>
<h2>2. How the service works</h2>
<p>Campaign owners submit advertising briefs and media for review, design and publication. Members may download personalized promotional material, choose whether to post it on WhatsApp Status, and submit the evidence required by the applicable campaign and earnings plan. A download, submission or screenshot does not by itself guarantee approval, reach, sales or earnings. Availability, capacity and eligibility conditions may apply.</p>
<p>You control what you post. You must follow WhatsApp's terms, applicable advertising rules and the law. [APP_NAME] is not WhatsApp or Meta and does not claim their endorsement. Clearly disclose paid or incentivized promotion where required. Do not mislead your audience or send unsolicited messages.</p>
<h2>3. Campaign tokens and charges</h2>
<p>Campaign tokens are advertising service credits, not money, a bank balance, cryptocurrency, an investment or a promise of financial return. They are separate from members' performance earnings. Token types, prices, currency and the submission-plus-reach quote are shown in the service. Review the quote before authorizing a submission. Video limits and other campaign requirements may also apply.</p>
<p>Tokens become available after payment is confirmed through the supported purchase process. Tokens may be reserved while an advert is reviewed or designed, used when it is published, or released if the submission is rejected. Changes to the final deliverable may require an updated quote and sufficient available tokens. A reservation release returns service credits; it is not a cash refund.</p>
<p>Only use the purchase methods authorized for the app or platform you are using. These Terms do not replace platform billing rules. Cancelling an unpaid purchase request does not refund an already settled payment. Contact support about failed charges, duplicate charges, unused credits or undelivered services. Refunds and remedies are assessed under the purchase terms, the relevant platform's rules and applicable law; nothing here removes a mandatory consumer right.</p>
<h2>4. Performance earnings, not pay per advert</h2>
<p>Eligible members earn under a performance plan, not a fixed reward for each advert. Under the multiplication model, a period's base amount is multiplied by the applicable views, consistency and qualified-referral/conversion multipliers, subject to the plan's caps and eligibility rules. Multipliers can be zero. Other calculation modes or metrics may be offered only under clearly communicated plan rules. A displayed maximum is a ceiling, not a guaranteed monthly income.</p>
<p>Views are assessed in the plan's configured ranges. Consistency considers eligible adverts and whether both required screenshots have been submitted and accepted within the required timing. Referrals count only when they meet the plan's qualification rules. Fake views, recycled evidence, altered screenshots, duplicate accounts and self-referrals do not qualify.</p>
<p>You may choose weekly or monthly payout where offered. The selected frequency, plan, verification window, minimum payout and monthly cap govern settlement. Period estimates can change while evidence is reviewed. Payment is recorded only after an actual payout is confirmed. A paid period is settled; a new earning period starts afresh, while historical statements and other outstanding periods remain separate. Payout processing may require identity/contact checks and a valid supported payment account. You are responsible for any taxes that apply to you.</p>
<h2>5. Verification and fair review</h2>
<p>Personalized media contains a tracking reference tied to the advert and the intended member. Do not submit another person's personalized image or screenshot. We check ownership references, duplicate evidence, timing and visible views. Uploaded screenshots may be processed by an AI service to identify WhatsApp Status evidence and extract view counts and tracking information. Automated analysis can make mistakes. Contact support to request human review of a rejection, suspected fraud or earnings decision.</p>
<p>We may hold a disputed item while investigating, explain the issue where lawful, and correct an incorrect result. Fraudulent activity may lead to rejection of affected evidence, reversal of improperly credited amounts or account suspension. Unrelated legitimate balances are not automatically forfeited merely because a dispute exists.</p>
<h2>6. Content, ownership and permitted use</h2>
<p>You retain ownership of content you provide and must have the rights and permissions needed to upload it, personalize it and distribute it for the campaign. You grant the operator a non-exclusive license to host, reproduce, resize, design, watermark, verify and distribute that content only as reasonably needed to provide the service. Members may use campaign media for the authorized campaign; this does not transfer the advertiser's intellectual property to them.</p>
<p>Do not submit unlawful, deceptive, infringing, hateful, sexually exploitative, harassing or dangerous content, or promote illegal goods or services. Obtain consent for identifiable people and do not upload private conversations, phone numbers or other people's personal information unnecessarily. We may reject or remove non-compliant content. Our software and branding remain protected; third-party materials belong to their respective owners.</p>
<h2>7. Device permissions and privacy</h2>
<p>[ACCESSIBILITY_DISCLOSURE]</p>
<p>Where a permission or sensitive-data feature requires separate disclosure and consent, that must be provided in the app; accepting these Terms is not a substitute. You can manage device permissions in your device settings. Some optional functions may not work when permission is refused. See the Privacy Policy for screenshots, providers, retention, international processing and your rights.</p>
<h2>8. Closing an account</h2>
<p>You can request deletion without reinstalling the app at our <a href="/delete-account">account and data deletion page</a>. We verify ownership before acting. Closure is not the same as simply disabling an account. Information no longer needed is deleted or anonymized; limited financial, dispute, security or legal records may need to be retained as described in the Privacy Policy. Outstanding legitimate payments or disputes are handled separately and do not justify indefinite retention of unrelated personal information.</p>
<p>We may restrict or suspend access for a material breach, fraud, security concerns or a legal requirement. Where appropriate, we will explain the restriction and provide a way to request review. A restriction does not remove your privacy rights.</p>
<h2>9. Service limits and your rights</h2>
<p>We take reasonable care but cannot guarantee uninterrupted access, error-free automated checks, campaign availability, third-party platform availability or a particular advertising result. Nothing excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, or removes statutory privacy, consumer or other mandatory rights. Participation does not by itself create employment, partnership or agency; any separate written agreement and applicable law still apply.</p>
<h2>10. Updates, questions and disputes</h2>
<p>The published version and effective date appear on this page. Material changes affecting your rights, data use or charges should be brought to your attention through an appropriate service notice before they apply where required. Changes do not retroactively rewrite a settled earnings period or an agreed purchase. Review new terms before accepting a materially changed service.</p>
<p>Contact the operator using the details on this page or the <a href="/privacy-request">support and privacy request form</a>. We aim to resolve concerns in good faith. Kenyan law applies, subject to any mandatory rights in your jurisdiction. You retain access to competent courts and regulators; these Terms do not require you to waive those rights.</p>
HTML;
    }

    private static function privacy(): string
    {
        return <<<'HTML'
<p>This Privacy Policy explains how [APP_NAME], operated by [OPERATOR_NAME], handles personal information when you create an account, manage a campaign, share adverts, submit performance evidence or contact us. Contact details and a privacy request form are available on this page.</p>
<h2>1. Information you provide</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Account and profile:</strong> name, username, email, phone number, password hash, gender, occupation, selected county/subcounty, verification status and referral identifiers. Selected location is profile information, not proof of continuous GPS tracking.</li><li><strong>Campaign information:</strong> business profiles, contact details, logos, advertising briefs, target-audience selections, images, video, text and media you upload for personalization.</li><li><strong>Performance evidence:</strong> WhatsApp Status screenshots, visible view counts, submission times, advert and member references, review outcomes and fraud indicators. Screenshots can include other people's information; avoid including private chats, contact lists or unrelated personal details.</li><li><strong>Transactions and earnings:</strong> token purchase quantities, amounts, currency, payment references, available/reserved/used credits, performance metrics, payout frequency, earnings periods, ledger entries, payout contact details and payment confirmations. We do not need your mobile-money PIN, card PIN or payment-account password.</li><li><strong>Support and privacy requests:</strong> the contact information, message and supporting information you choose to provide, plus request handling records.</li></ul>
<h2>2. Technical information and permissions</h2>
<p>The service processes authentication tokens, sessions, request/security logs and device push-notification tokens. Session and server records may include IP address, user agent, timestamps and error information. Authentication and security cookies support the website and admin area. App permissions depend on the Android release; access to images or storage should be limited to the feature you choose to use.</p>
<p>[ACCESSIBILITY_DISCLOSURE]</p>
<p>A privacy policy does not replace a separate in-app permission disclosure or affirmative consent where required. We do not need your private chat history to verify an advert. Do not share passwords or OTPs with another person. Optional permission choices can be changed through device settings.</p>
<h2>3. Why information is used</h2>
<ul><li>Create and secure accounts; send phone verification codes; maintain contact and account status.</li><li>Operate campaigns, select relevant opportunities using supplied profile/audience information, deliver personalized media and send service notifications.</li><li>Verify advert ownership and screenshot evidence, calculate views and consistency, qualify referrals, calculate period earnings, and manage token reservations, purchases and payouts.</li><li>Prevent fraud, abuse and duplicate claims; investigate disputes; provide human review and support.</li><li>Respond to privacy requests, maintain necessary financial/audit records and comply with applicable legal obligations.</li></ul>
<p>Where applicable under Kenya's Data Protection Act, processing relies on performance of the service agreement, compliance with legal obligations, proportionate legitimate interests such as security and fraud prevention, or specific consent where required. You may object to relevant processing or withdraw consent without affecting processing already lawfully carried out. Information necessary for account security, a campaign or a payout may be needed to provide that function.</p>
<h2>4. Personalized images and referral relationships</h2>
<p>Downloaded/stamped media can contain an invisible watermark, a signed reference, a visible tracking code or a legacy QR reference. Server-side records associate the reference with an advert and its intended member for ownership and anti-fraud checks. A reference is not anonymous to the operator, and hidden watermarking is not a guarantee that information cannot be extracted. Publicly posting the media makes the image available to your audience and the platform you choose.</p>
<p>Referral codes link the referring account with qualifying activity of a referred member. They support the performance calculation and abuse checks; they do not require access to your phone's address book. Do not upload someone else's personal details without authorization.</p>
<h2>5. Service providers and other disclosures</h2>
<p>We do not sell your personal information. Information is disclosed as needed to provide the functions below, resolve disputes or comply with the law:</p>
<ul><li><strong>TalkSasa:</strong> receives the destination phone number and SMS content to deliver OTP and service messages.</li><li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> receives uploaded screenshot image content and verification instructions for AI analysis of WhatsApp evidence, view counts and tracking information. The screenshot may contain any personal information left visible in it. Avoid unrelated information before uploading.</li><li><strong>Google Firebase:</strong> supports push notifications using device notification tokens and message content.</li><li><strong>Hosting, storage and authorized staff:</strong> process account, uploaded-media and operational information to run, secure and support the service with appropriate access restrictions.</li><li><strong>Payment providers:</strong> process the details needed for a supported purchase or payout. The specific provider and transaction information are made available in the payment flow or on request. A payment reference recorded in our system is not a claim that the operator is a bank or licensed payment service provider.</li><li><strong>Legal and safety recipients:</strong> information may be disclosed where legally required or reasonably necessary to investigate fraud, protect rights or address a security incident, subject to applicable law.</li></ul>
<p>WhatsApp/Meta and any platform on which you choose to publish operate under their own terms and privacy policies. Do not assume their handling is controlled by [APP_NAME].</p>
<h2>6. International processing and security</h2>
<p>Hosting and providers such as OpenAI and Google may process information outside Kenya. Before using a transfer route, the operator must establish an applicable lawful transfer basis and appropriate safeguards under Kenyan law. Contact us for the relevant recipients, locations and safeguards; this policy is not a representation that every provider is located in Kenya or that a particular certification exists.</p>
<p>Security measures include password hashing, expiring/attempt-limited phone verification codes, authenticated account access, staff authorization and ownership checks for evidence. Production connections must use HTTPS and access to stored media and logs must be controlled. No service can promise absolute security. Report a suspected exposure to the privacy contact promptly.</p>
<h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2>
<p>[RETENTION_POLICY]</p>
<p>Request account and associated data deletion using the <a href="/delete-account">deletion page</a>, even if you have uninstalled the app. We will take proportionate steps to verify account ownership before deletion; submitting the form alone does not immediately remove an account. We distinguish deletion/anonymization from temporary suspension or a recoverable admin deletion. If specific records must be retained for a legitimate legal, financial, dispute or fraud-prevention purpose, we explain the category, reason and retention period. Such exceptions do not permit retaining unrelated personal information indefinitely.</p>
<h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2>
<p>Subject to applicable law, you can ask to access or correct your information, delete information no longer lawfully needed, restrict or object to processing, withdraw consent, obtain eligible portable data, and request human review of a significant automated decision. AI verification can be wrong; contact us about a rejected screenshot, an incorrect view count or an earnings decision. Use the <a href="/privacy-request">privacy request form</a> or the contact details below. Never send your password, mobile-money PIN or a live OTP in that form.</p>
<p>If you remain concerned, you may complain to Kenya's <a href="https://www.odpc.go.ke/">Office of the Data Protection Commissioner</a> or another competent regulator.</p>
<h2>9. Adults only</h2>
<p>The service is intended for adults aged 18 and over. Do not register a child or upload a child's information without an appropriate lawful basis. If you believe a child has an account or their information has been submitted improperly, contact us so we can investigate and take appropriate action.</p>
<h2>10. Changes and contact</h2>
<p>The effective date, publication date and version appear on this page. Material changes to data use require an appropriate notice and, where necessary, renewed consent before the new processing starts. Contact [OPERATOR_NAME] using the details below or our privacy request form.</p>
HTML;
    }
}
